The Rust standard library
Used by:
  std, core, alloc and the crates they bundle, of Rust 1.99.1
================================================================================

The library is built with Rust 1.99.1 and statically links its standard library: std, core and alloc, and the
crates they bundle, such as hashbrown, compiler_builtins, gimli, addr2line, object, miniz_oxide, adler2,
rustc-demangle, memchr, cfg-if, libc, std_detect, unwind and panic_unwind. They are licensed under
"MIT OR Apache-2.0", the Rust project's own licence, except for the parts that the Rust project's COPYRIGHT file
names under other permissive licences. The texts are in the Rust project's repository:

